        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "5f2eebb3-b6dd-51c2-9aa9-eae6d81b618e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Cussonia, Ternstroemia, Seemannaralia gerrardii\n- Places: Africa, South Africa, Mascarene Islands, Asia, the Americas, Ceuta\n- Buildings: Ceuta Cathedral\n- Organizations: Roman Catholic Church\n\nFacts:\n- Cussonia originated in Africa and has its center of distribution in South Africa and the Mascarene Islands.\n- Ternstroemia is distributed in tropical and subtropical regions of Africa, Asia, and the Americas.\n- Seemannaralia gerrardii was originally included in the genus Cussonia.\n- Ceuta Cathedral, also called the Cathedral of St Mary of the Assumption, is a Roman Catholic church in the Spanish city of Ceuta on the northwest coast of Africa.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
